  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. It replaces a record naming the owner as reviewer, because that record's fingerprint no longer matched; that record stays in git history. Read client.request_construction and http_profile.evidence_block_carriage (body/mod.rs has no diff). mcp-re-client-core/src/request.rs replaced build_signed_request, build_signed_request_with_signer, build_signed_notification, build_signed_notification_with_signer and build_signed_tool_call by build_signed_message and build_signed_message_with_signer over one McpMessage, with McpMessage::tool_call for the common call. Compared with the old production code: check_preconditions runs continuation-on-a-notification first, then the audience cross-check, the 22-character nonce floor and expires-after-created, the same order and the same errors as before (the old notification entry points rejected the continuation before the shared core ran the other three); the body is built from id, jsonrpc, method and params alone, with the id key omitted rather than null; HttpRequestEvidenceBlock::validate runs before signing; signing goes through sign_request_full or the signer closure with a RequestSignature carrying the same key id, created, expires and nonce. The tests changed only to call build_signed_message with McpMessage::new; all 15 cited tests resolve and keep their expectations. The request is now built through one entry point rather than five, which narrows the seam the claim describes. The claim holds. The mutation lane was not run, and no test was run. Evidence class as registered (V0).",
